            <ArticleTitle>Retroperitoneal fibrosis: unusual cause of low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>735-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Retroperitoneal fibrosis (RPF) is an uncommon collagen vascular disease with a male predominance. Back pain with no specific radiation pattern is common, and bilateral obstructive uropathy, potentially reversible, is frequently associated with RPF. We report a case of RPF and review its diagnosis and management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
